From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sailfish sweet port <bigisoft@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (hybris) Map droid-hybris/vendor/bin to the vendor section

droid-hal ships Android binaries under /usr/libexec/droid-hybris, and 0001
maps /usr/libexec/droid-hybris/system/bin to the "system" linker section.
That is wrong for binaries which are vendor-side in AOSP: they end up linked
against /system/lib64/libbinder.so instead of /vendor/lib64/libbinder.so.

vndservicemanager is the case that matters. Built as a vendor module
(Android.bp: vendor: true, -DVENDORSERVICEMANAGER=1) but executed from a
"system" directory, it gets the system libbinder and therefore system binder
stability, while every vendor client uses the vendor libbinder. libbinder then
rejects addService() locally, before the transaction is ever written to
/dev/vndbinder -- silently, because ServiceManager::canAddService() does not
log a denial and QTI's QService::init() only reports via ALOGD_IF.

Observed on Redmi Note 10 Pro (sweet), hybris-23.2 / Android 16: /dev/vndbinder
held zero services, so the QTI composer could not publish display.qservice,
HWCSession::Init() failed with -EINVAL, android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.4
-service exited in a restart loop, the HIDL composer never registered, and
lipstick blocked forever in IComposer::getService(). The screen never left the
bootloader splash.

Note the matching is per parent directory (linker_config.cpp file_is_in_dir),
so a separate directory is required -- a longer path prefix does not work.
---
 contents/configuration/baseconfig.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/contents/configuration/baseconfig.cc b/contents/configuration/baseconfig.cc
index 468e653..0fc7cde 100644
--- a/contents/configuration/baseconfig.cc
+++ b/contents/configuration/baseconfig.cc
@@ -82,6 +82,12 @@ android::linkerconfig::modules::Configuration CreateBaseConfiguration(
       // binaries in APKs
       {Var("PRODUCT") + "/app/", "system"},
       {"/usr/libexec/droid-hybris/system/bin", "system"},
+      // (hybris) Vendor-side binaries that droid-hal ships outside /vendor still
+      // have to be linked against the vendor copies of libbinder/libc++/libutils.
+      // vndservicemanager in particular: run from a "system" directory it loads
+      // /system/lib64/libbinder.so, gets system binder stability, and then rejects
+      // every addService() from a vendor process before it reaches the wire.
+      {"/usr/libexec/droid-hybris/vendor/bin", "vendor"},
   };
 
   sections.emplace_back(BuildSystemSection(ctx));
